{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788496559509628001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"lovesick-missing-andeancat","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"144ac8303644cceddf941cdf47089d08c88dd81876f373c1c70ce3d3b7d3c8f0","event_uuid":"f1f765d6-4983-4a86-9307-8d7f629dff11","position":{"commit_sha":"271df927aa8ebee05c3014e082cca451a0df08f8","position":"1788489907724048001-f1f765d6-4983-4a86-9307-8d7f629dff11"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d8bc1d20eb18ae64ac96ff3b61bc953ae7235ac2ed92b660fe783c56980f4062","event_uuid":"982b68a7-3047-4721-8ac8-10593ea32137","position":{"commit_sha":"27396d0226f0c1efe01af1719288426e8932f527","position":"1788489918798748001-982b68a7-3047-4721-8ac8-10593ea32137"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788489907724048001,"creation_channel":"python","deps":[{"link_uuid":"982b68a7-3047-4721-8ac8-10593ea32137","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"67aa-eb04-8814-4975"}],"description":"## Context\n\nThe fixture-admission runner (`src/rebar/llm/evals/fixture_admission.py`, epic REB-693 / 67aa) SCOPES OUT container criteria (G3/G4/decomp-shape) as `container-material-unrecoverable`: the replay corpus (`src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/corpus.py`) persists a review's children as bare ticket-id STRINGS only (`_child_ids`), with no per-child title/description. But the LIVE plan-review container finder reads each child's full title/description at review time (`context_assembly.py` fetches every child via `show_ticket`), and G3's coverage-discharge cannot fire on a title-only roster (`container_stage.py`). So a container case rehydrated from the corpus would run the finder over an IMPOVERISHED roster — an admit/drift verdict UNFAITHFUL to history. `material_fingerprint` hashes children by id only (`material_diff.py`), so it cannot detect the loss.\n\n## Approach\n\nExtend the corpus sidecar row to persist per-child at-review `{canonical_id, title, description}` (reconstruct each child's title+description from its OWN event history at `review_ts`, reusing the `_reconstruct_material` machinery already used for the parent description), and rehydrate those into the `{ticket_id, title, description}` records the container finder consumes. When a child's at-review material is unrecoverable, withhold that case to drift as unrecoverable rather than running the finder over a degraded roster. Then REMOVE the container scope-out guard in `fixture_admission.run_admission` and re-run a live admission over G3/G4/decomp-shape to mint faithful specs.\n\n## Scope\n\n`corpus.py` (per-child material reconstruction + persistence), `fixture_admission.py` (drop the container scope-out once corpus is faithful), the container eval specs re-minted by a live run.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The corpus sidecar row persists per-child `{canonical_id, title, description}` reconstructed at `review_ts`; a unit test over synthetic child histories asserts the reconstructed title/description match the child's state as of the review.\n- [ ] The admission runner rehydrates container children WITH title/description and dispatches G3/G4 to the finder (no longer withheld as container-material-unrecoverable); a held-out test asserts a container must-fire case reproduces over the faithful roster.\n- [ ] A child whose at-review material is unrecoverable withholds that case to drift as unrecoverable (not a degraded-roster finder call).\n- [ ] A live admission run mints faithful G3/G4 specs; ledger records the spend ≤ cap.\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n`make lint`/`make typecheck`/`make test` pass; container specs re-minted faithfully.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"2340-d9a9-2e49-4c18","ticket_type":"task","title":"Persist per-child at-review material so container criteria (G3/G4) admit faithfully","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f1f765d6-4983-4a86-9307-8d7f629dff11","982b68a7-3047-4721-8ac8-10593ea32137"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788496559509628001,"uuid":"a1df97dc-65f7-4918-8c63-c6352f814264"}